From 850bd180d2be2825db9c80100b4239261bf1b00a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EthanCao <ethan.caoq@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:21:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ccrg: report alerts, multi-source Generate YAML, origin
 popover

- Restore HTMLReportGeneratorImpl and overall-html-fragment.html from
  develop/deperacted-version: release/release-ccrg did not compile
  (PdfController imports HTMLReportGeneratorImpl) and the Overall tab was empty.
- Report alerts (ConfigAlertService, ccrg.alerts.* in application.yml):
  another environment's address and plain-text secrets (critical), watched
  keys that differ (high), accepted differences. Banner + Alerts tab in
  report-html-export-index, severity badges and "Alerts only" filter in the
  Overall Comparison; secrets masked in the Alerts tab.
- Origin popover: one delegated listener and one popover at a time
  (fragments/origin-popover-script.html) instead of an eager popover per
  line with click/hover/focus triggers and stacked 20 s timers.
- Generate YAML: several sources merged in order, the later source wins a
  key; POST /prompt/generate-yaml/merge returns every conflicting key. The
  page edits a list of sources (add / duplicate / reorder / remove, two per
  row on wide screens); the saved form is now an array (old format still loads).
- Tests: ConfigAlertServiceTest, HtmlReportAlertsRenderTest,
  EffectiveYamlServiceTest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
